  data:  # 5722
    kind: invariant  # 5722
    title: "Python emits no call edge for a bare-name call it cannot resolve, so a catalogued section-4 terminating summary (print) can never be applied"  # 5722
    status: violated  # 5722
    priority: 1  # 5722
    parent:  # 5722
    tags:  # 5722
    - taint  # 5722
    - python  # 5722
    - analyzer  # 5722
    - adr_0017  # 5722
    isbefore: []  # 5722
    duplicate_of: []  # 5722
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 5722
    pr_ref:  # 5722
    description: "MEASURED 2026-08-16 on dev 0d305fe0e4 while re-measuring INV-busis's escape-cause\nbreakdown. This is the LARGEST single cause of section 3a escapes on hypergumbo's\nown tree (10 of 21 CALL-node escape sites, 47.6%), and INV-busis attributes that\nbucket to INV-mumov, which is the wrong owner -- INV-mumov is about attribute-chain\nreceivers, and none of these ten are that shape.\n\nTHE DEFECT. The Python analyzer emits NO call edge for a bare-name call whose\ncallee it cannot resolve in-project. Measured on a fixture, production\nanalyze_python:\n\n    helper(x)                 bare name DEFINED in file    EDGE\n    os.remove(x)              module-qualified             EDGE\n    x.decode()                simple-name receiver         EDGE\n    open(p)                   builtin, WI-mitul's fix      EDGE\n    print(x)                  builtin                      none\n    len(items)                builtin                      none\n    input()                   builtin                      none\n    eval(x)                   builtin                      none\n    getattr(x, \"y\")           builtin                      none\n    undefined_fn(x)           unresolvable bare name       none\n    items[i].startswith(x)    SUBSCRIPT receiver           none\n\nMECHANISM, read in code. py.py's terminal bare-Name arm (~line 6377) emits\npython:builtins:0-0:<name>:unresolved only when the name is in\nBUILTIN_CONSTRUCTOR_NAMES -- \"bare rows that are REAL builtins\", derived from the\nio_primitives catalogue. So the permitting set is \"builtins that are catalogued\nI/O PRIMITIVES\". print / input / eval / len / getattr are not I/O primitives, so\nthey are not in the set, so they emit nothing. Every other analyzer in the fleet\nemits an unresolved edge here via make_unresolved_edge.\n\nWHY IT IS A CLASS AND NOT A LIST OF BUILTINS. WI-mitul (done, PR #385) closed\nexactly one door -- open() -- by adding it to that table. The closure note says\nso: \"for bare builtin I/O constructors (open) via EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES\".\nThe gate is a per-name allowlist keyed on a catalogue built for a DIFFERENT\npurpose (I/O classification), so every non-I/O callee that needs an edge for a\nnon-I/O reason is invisible, and each one has to be discovered and added\nseparately. Filed as a class per LIVE.md rule 10 (one door closed is not the\nclass closed) rather than as \"also add print\".\n\nTHE CONSEQUENCE THAT MAKES IT P1, and it is not about I/O at all. ADR-0017\nsection 4 function summaries are how the section 3a walk decides a use TERMINATES\nthe taint rather than propagating it -- the difference between an accounted-for\nstep and an escape. The section 4 index holds a terminating summary for print\nunder BOTH keys:\n\n    builtins.print -> FunctionSummary(side_effect=True, param_to_return={})\n    print          -> FunctionSummary(side_effect=True, param_to_return={})\n\nand it can never be applied, because no edge is ever emitted at a print() call\nsite, so the callee never reaches callees_at. A catalogued terminating summary\nthat the walk structurally cannot consult is the section 3a blocker INV-busis\nexists to name. Same for any future summary keyed on a bare-name builtin.\n\nSCOPE NOT MEASURED, stated so nobody reads more into this than was checked:\n  - Python only. I did not check whether other analyzers withhold bare-name\n    unresolved edges (the ones I sampled emit).\n  - The subscript-receiver shape (items[i].startswith(x)) is in the same\n    \"emits nothing\" bucket but is a DIFFERENT mechanism from the bare-name arm;\n    it may want its own fix and is not covered by the statement above.\n  - I did not measure the corpus-wide edge-count delta a fix would produce.\n    It will be large and positive, and per INV-linub's direction discipline it\n    must be measured on FINDINGS and on BOTH signs before shipping: more\n    callees_at feeds section 7a sanitizer registration, and a barrier False\n    earns 'sanitized' and DROPS a flow (#214). An emission fix here can\n    manufacture suppression."  # 5722
    fields:  # 5722
      statement: "Every call site whose callee carries an ADR-0017 section 4 function summary must produce a call edge, or the summary can never be consulted and the section 3a walk must treat an accounted-for step as an escape. VIOLATED for Python bare-name calls: print/input/eval/len/getattr emit no edge, while the section 4 index holds a terminating summary for print under both 'print' and 'builtins.print'."  # 5722
      root_cause: "py.py's terminal bare-Name call arm emits python:builtins:0-0:<name>:unresolved only for names in BUILTIN_CONSTRUCTOR_NAMES, a set derived from the io_primitives catalogue -- i.e. the permitting condition is 'this builtin is a catalogued I/O primitive'. Callees needing an edge for a non-I/O reason (a section 4 summary) are outside that set by construction. WI-mitul added open() to the same table rather than removing the coupling, so the gate remains a per-name allowlist keyed on an unrelated catalogue."  # 5722
