  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nRE-VERIFIED AT TIP, STILL VIOLATED. This item had zero discussion entries; recording the independent reproduction. Production analyze_python on a single fixture file, dev 11a240f83d -- one run, so the emitting and non-emitting shapes share every other condition:\n\n    EDGE EMITTED                       NO EDGE\n      helper(x)   bare name in file      print(x)      builtin\n      os.remove(x)  module-qualified     len(x)        builtin\n      obj.decode()  simple receiver      undefined_fn(x)  unresolvable\n      obj.related.create(x)  attr chain  x[0].startswith('a')  subscript receiver\n\nTHE SUBSCRIPT-RECEIVER SHAPE IS A SECOND MEMBER, and it is in this item's scope by mechanism (the receiver is not a resolvable name) but is not named in the title. INV-busis records it as 'a distinct subscript-receiver shape'; it should be decided here whether this item owns it or it gets its own filing, because a fix aimed only at bare NAMES will leave it.\n\nThe consequence INV-busis attaches to this item is unchanged and is the reason it is P1: the section 4 index holds a TERMINATING summary for print under both keys (builtins.print and print), and the walk cannot apply it because no edge reaches callees_at -- so the canonical 'the taint ends here' use is counted as an ESCAPE."  # a54b
